In React, the equivalent of a WPF ListView is a Grid or a Table component.

The Grid component in React is a flexible layout component that can be used to create a grid of items with different sizes and gaps between them. It can be used to create a ListView-like widget.

To use the Grid component, you need to import it from the 'react-grid-layout' package. Here's an example of how you can use it to create a simple ListView:
```javascript
import React from 'react';
import { Grid } from 'react-grid-layout';

const items = [
  { id: 1, text: 'Item 1' },
  { id: 2, text: 'Item 2' },
  { id: 3, text: 'Item 3' },
];

const ListView = () => {
  return (
    <Grid
      columnDefinitions={[
        { width: 1/3, locked: true },
        { width: 2/3 },
      ]}
      rowDefinitions={[
        { height: 1 },
        { height: 4 },
        { height: 1 },
      ]}
      items={items}
    >
      {item => (
        <div>
          <div>{item.id}</div>
          <div>{item.text}</div>
        </div>
      )}
    </Grid>
  );
};

export default ListView;
```
In this example, we define a simple list of items with their IDs and texts. We then use the Grid component to create a grid of items with a fixed first column, a scrollable middle column, and a fixed last column. We pass in the column and row definitions as props to the Grid component.

Finally, we map over the items array and render a div for each item that contains its ID and text.

Note that this is just a simple example, and you can customize the Grid component to fit your specific requirements.

