Here is a sample RMAN script to perform a full database backup of Oracle 11.2:

```sql
# Full Database Backup

connect target sys/password@orcl 
# Connect to target database as sysdba

run {
  allocate channel ch1 type disk;
  backup incremental level 0 database format '/backup/db_%T_%U';
  release channel ch1;
}

# Backup database to /backup/db_<timestamp>_%U 
# %T = timestamp, %U = backup piece number

delete noprompt obsolete;
# Delete obsolete backups

delete noprompt expired backup;  
# Delete expired backups

report obsolete;
# List obsolete backups

report expired backup;
# List expired backups

exit;
```

The key steps are:

- Connect to target database as sysdba 
- Allocate RMAN channel 
- Perform level 0 incremental backup (full)
- Release channel
- Delete obsolete and expired backups
- Report on obsolete and expired backups
- Exit

This will perform a full backup of the entire database to the /backup directory with file names containing timestamp and backup piece number. Old backups are deleted and listed to confirm.

