When the function is called with a value of 0 for `` bar ``, the value of `` x `` will be used as the default value for `` bar ``. If a value of 0 is not provided for `` bar ``, then the default value of 5 will be used instead.

For example, the following code will call the function with `` bar = 0 `` and `` x = 5 ``, resulting in the output of `` 5 ``:


