```javascript
function deminifyCode(code) {
  // First, remove all comments from the code
  code = code.replace(//\*[\s\S]*?\*\//g, '');

  // Next, collapse all consecutive whitespace characters
  code = code.replace(/\s+/g, ' ');

  // Unescape any escaped characters
  code = code.replace(/\\[^\s]/g, function(character) {
    return character.replace('\\', '');
  });

  // Finally, remove the line terminators
  code = code.replace(/(?:\r\n?|\n)/g, ' ');

  return code;
}
```
You can call this function for each file you want to de-minify, passing in the code as a string argument. The function will return the de-minified code as a string that you can use to replace the original code in your files.

