```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int n, i, isPrime = 1;
    printf("Enter a number: ");
    scanf("%d", &n);

    for (i = 2; i <= n/2; ++i) {
        if (n % i == 0) {
            isPrime = 0;
            break;
        }
    }

    if (isPrime == 1)
        printf("%d is a prime number.", n);
    else
        printf("%d is not a prime number.", n);

    return 0; 
}
```

This program does the following:

1. Prompts the user to enter a number
2. Stores the number in the variable n
3. Initializes a flag isPrime to 1 (true) and a counter i to 2 
4. Loops from i = 2 to n/2. We only need to check up to the square root of n.
5. Checks if n is divisible by i. If so, sets isPrime to 0 (false) and breaks out of the loop. 
6. If isPrime is still 1, prints that n is a prime number. Otherwise prints that it's not prime.
7. Returns 0 to indicate successful execution.

