How can I return plain text instead of view?

To return plain text from a controller method in CodeIgniter 4, simply return a string instead of calling `view()`:

```php
class Home extends BaseController
{
    public function index()
    {
        return 'Hello world!';
    }
}
```

This will send a response with the string content and a `text/html` content type.

If you want to specify a different content type, use the `setContentType()` method:

```php
public function index()
{
    $this->setContentType('text/plain');
    return 'Hello world!'; 
}
```

This will send a `text/plain` content type with the string content.

So in summary, to return plain text (or any raw string content) from a controller, simply return the string directly. You can also set the content type explicitly using `setContentType()` if needed.

