This is happening because CodeIgniter 4's dependency injection container needs to be explicitly told about the IWelcomMessageProvider interface and the StubWelcomeMessageProvider implementation.

To fix this, you'll need to do two things:

1. Register the IWelcomMessageProvider interface in Config/Services.php:

```php
public static function welcomeMessageProviderInterface($getShared = true) 
{
    return IWelcomMessageProvider::class; 
}
```

2. Bind the StubWelcomeMessageProvider implementation to that interface:

```php 
public static function welcomeMessageProvider($getShared = true) 
{
    return static::getSharedInstance(StubWelcomeMessageProvider::class, static::welcomeMessageProviderInterface());
}
```

So your full Config/Services.php will look like this:

```php
<?php 

namespace Config;

use App\Controllers\IWelcomMessageProvider;
use Services\StubWelcomeMessageProvider;

class Services 
{
    public static function welcomeMessageProviderInterface($getShared = true) 
    {
        return IWelcomMessageProvider::class; 
    }

    public static function welcomeMessageProvider($getShared = true) 
    {
        return static::getSharedInstance(StubWelcomeMessageProvider::class, static::welcomeMessageProviderInterface());
    }
}
```

This tells the DI container that it should inject the StubWelcomeMessageProvider implementation whenever the IWelcomMessageProvider interface is requested.

