The `@mixin` is a feature in CSS that allows you to define a mixin, which is a reusable piece of CSS code that can be included in multiple stylesheets. A mixin is essentially a function that takes one or more parameters and returns a CSS value. It can be used to define a set of styles that can be easily applied to multiple elements or stylesheets, without having to repeat the same code over and over again.

For example, you can define a mixin that sets the background color of an element, and then use that mixin in multiple stylesheets to quickly apply a consistent background color to different elements.

Here is an example of a simple `@mixin` in CSS:
```css
@mixin blue-bg {
  background-color: blue;
}
```
This mixin can then be used in other stylesheets like this:
```css
.my-element {
  @include blue-bg;
}
```
This would apply the `blue-bg` mixin to the element with the class `my-element`, setting its background color to blue.

