using UnityEngine;

public class EnemyMovement : MonoBehaviour
{
    public float speed = 1.0f;
    public float timeBetweenDirectionChanges = 2.0f;

    private float currentDirection = 0.0f;

    void Update()
    {
        // Update the current direction of the enemy
        currentDirection = Mathf.Sin(currentDirection * Mathf.PI / 60.0f) * speed;

        // Move the enemy in the current direction
        transform.position += transform.right * currentDirection * Time.deltaTime;

        // Change the direction of the enemy after a set time
        float elapsedTime = Time.time - lastDirectionChange;
        if (elapsedTime > timeBetweenDirectionChanges)
        {
            lastDirectionChange = Time.time;
            currentDirection = (currentDirection + 3.0f) % 4.0f;
        }
    }
}
```
This script uses the sin() function to create a repeating pattern of moving forward to the left and right. The time between direction changes is controlled by the `timeBetweenDirectionChanges` variable. The `currentDirection` variable keeps track of the current direction the enemy is moving in, and is updated every frame. The `transform.position` property is used to move the enemy in the current direction. Finally, the `lastDirectionChange` variable keeps track of when the enemy last changed direction, and is used to determine when to change the direction again.

