The issue is that the useEffect hook has a dependency on tasks, which causes it to rerun whenever tasks changes. But when it reruns, it sets tasks again, causing an infinite loop.

To fix this, you need to remove tasks from the dependency array:

```js
useEffect(() => {
    axios
        .get<Task[]>('http://localhost:3000/tasks.json')
        .then(response => setTasks(response.data))
}, [])  // Empty dependency array
```

