To invoke the `Deserialize<T>` method dynamically using caching, you can create a caching object that stores the serialized instances of the `T` type and invoke the `Deserialize<T>` method on each stored instance. Here's an example of how you can do this:
```csharp
public static class Caching
{
    private static ReadOnlySequence<byte> _byteSequenceCache = new ReadOnlySequence<byte>();

    public static T Deserialize<T>(in ReadOnlySequence<byte> byteSequence, MessagePackSerializerOptions? options = null, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
    {
        if (byteSequence == null)
        {
            throw new ArgumentNullException("byteSequence");
        }

        var serializedBytes = byteSequence.AsReadOnly();
        var deserializer = new MessagePackSerializer<T>(options?? defaultMessagePackSerializerOptions);

        if ( serializedBytes.Length!= deserializer.Serialize( serializedBytes ) )
        {
            throw new ArgumentException("Invalid sequence of bytes", "byteSequence");
        }

        foreach (var serializedInstance in serializedBytes)
        {
            if (_byteSequenceCache.TryGetValue( serializedInstance )
                &&!_byteSequenceCache.Contains( serializedInstance ))
            {
                _byteSequenceCache.Add( serializedInstance );
                Deserialize<T>( serializedInstance, deserializer, cancellationToken );
            }
        }

        return deserializer.Deserialize<T>( serializedBytes, cancellationToken );
    }
}
```
In this example, the `Caching` class uses a cache object `_byteSequenceCache` to store the serialized instances of the `T` type. The `Deserialize<T>` method checks if the `byteSequence` is null, and if so, it throws an exception. If the `byteSequence` is not null, the method uses the `MessagePackSerializer<T>` to deserialize the `byteSequence` and stores the resulting serialized instance in the cache. The method then iterates through the cache and deserializes each stored instance. If a stored instance is not found in the cache, the method adds it to the cache using the `TryGetValue` method. Finally, the method invokes the `Deserialize<T>` method on each stored instance using the cache.

