You're right, in this case the map is essentially being used as an object! Since the keys are strings (Roman numerals), either a map or object would work fine here.

Some reasons a map was probably chosen:

1. Semantic meaning - Map conveys more clearly that this is a lookup table of key-value pairs.

2. Future proofing - If in the future the keys become more complex (objects, functions, etc), a map would still work whereas an object would not.

But you're correct that in this specific implementation, an object would work identically:

