Here is a C# function that sorts menu items alphabetically:

```csharp
public Menu SortMenuAlphabetically(Menu menu)
{
    List<MenuItem> items = menu.Items.ToList();
    items.Sort((x, y) => string.Compare(x.Text, y.Text));
    menu.Items.Clear();
    foreach (MenuItem item in items)
    {
        menu.Items.Add(item);
    }
    return menu;
}
```

This function does the following:

- Gets the list of MenuItem objects from the Menu using .Items.ToList()
- Sorts the list alphabetically using .Sort() and a string comparison lambda expression 
- Clears the original Menu.Items list 
- Adds the sorted MenuItem objects back to the Menu.Items list
- Returns the sorted Menu

