2. Pointers: Pointers are variables that store the memory address of another variable. You'll need to use pointers to traverse the array and swap the elements of the string.
3. Swapping: Swapping is the process of exchanging the values of two variables. In this case, you'll need to swap the characters at each index of the string.

Here's an example of how you can reverse a string in C using these concepts:
```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

void reverse_string(char* str) {
    int length = strlen(str);
    for (int i = 0; i < length / 2; i++) {
        char temp = str[i];
        str[i] = str[length - i - 1];
        str[length - i - 1] = temp;
    }
}

