.grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  height: 100vh;
}

.top {
  grid-row: 1 / 2;
}

.bottom {
  grid-row: 2 / 3; 
}
```

This will create a grid `div` with two columns of equal size (1fr) and set its height to 100% of the viewport height (100vh).

Then the `.top` item will occupy the first row, and `.bottom` item will occupy the second row, effectively dividing the grid into top and bottom halves.

The HTML would be:

```html
<div class="grid">
  <div class="top">Top content</div>
  <div class="bottom">Bottom content</div> 
</div>
```

