val sortedArr = quickSort(arr)
println(sortedArr) // prints [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
```
This implementation of quick sort uses Kotlin flows to handle the asynchronous nature of the partitioning and sorting operations. The function creates a channel to communicate the result of the sort, and starts two coroutines to handle the left and right halves of the partition.

In the left half coroutine, the elements less than the pivot are sorted and sent to the result channel. In the right half coroutine, the elements greater than the pivot are recursively sorted using the quick sort function, and the sorted result is sent to the result channel.

The function then waits for the partitions to finish sorting and receives the sorted result from the result channel. If either partition fails to sort, the function returns the failed partition. Otherwise, the function concatenates the two sorted halves and returns the result.

