// Another thread can now call Wait() and acquire the permit
```

Calling Release() on the semaphore "posts" a permit back to the semaphore, allowing another thread waiting in Wait() to proceed.

A full example of using Wait(), Release() and posting to a semaphore would be:
```csharp
// Create a semaphore with a NAME_1 count of 3
Semaphore semaphore = new Semaphore(3, 3);

void DoWork()
{
    // Wait for a permit
    semaphore.Wait();  

    // Do some work...
    Debug.Log("Doing work...");

    // Release the permit, posting back to the semaphore
    semaphore.Release();  
}

// Thread 1
new Thread(DoWork).Start();

// Thread 2 
new Thread(DoWork).Start();  

// Thread 3 
new Thread(DoWork).Start();  

// Thread 4 will block here until a permit is released
new Thread(DoWork).Start();  
```

This will allow 3 threads to run DoWork() simultaneously. The 4th thread will block in Wait() until one of the first 3 threads posts a permit back to the semaphore.

