To calculate a trendline from an array of OHCLV values in JavaScript, you can use the following steps:

1. First, sort the array of OHCLV values in descending order. This will give you the highest values at the beginning of the array and the lowest values at the end.
2. Next, calculate the mean of the first and last values in the array. These values represent the minimum and maximum OHCLV values.
3. Calculate the mean of the remaining values in the array. This will give you the average OHCLV value.
4. Calculate the slope of the line that connects the minimum and maximum OHCLV values. This represents the steepness of the trendline.
5. If the slope is positive, the trendline is increasing. If the slope is negative, the trendline is decreasing. If the slope is close to 0, the trendline is relatively flat.

Here's an example of how you can implement this in JavaScript:
```javascript
function calcTrendline(ohclvArray) {
  ohclvArray.sort(function(a, b) {
    return b - a;
  });

  const firstValue = ohclvArray[0];
  const lastValue = ohclvArray[ohclvArray.length - 1];
  const numValues = ohclvArray.length - 1;
  const meanValue = (ohclvArray[ohclvArray.length - numValues] + ohclvArray[0]) / 2;
  const slope = (firstValue - lastValue) / numValues;

  return {
    slope: slope,
    isIncreasing: slope > 0,
    isDecreasing: slope < 0,
    isFlat: Math.abs(slope) < 0.01
  };
}

