```c
void bubbleSort(int arr[], int n) {
    int i, j, temp;
    for (i = 0; i < n-1; i++) {
        for (j = 0; j < n-i-1; j++) {
            if (arr[j] > arr[j+1]) {
                temp = arr[j];
                arr[j] = arr[j+1];
                arr[j+1] = temp;
            }
        }
    }
}
```

This function takes in an array and its size as arguments, and sorts the elements in the array in ascending order. The bubble sort algorithm works by repeatedly iterating through the array and comparing adjacent elements, swapping them if they are in the wrong order. The algorithm repeats this process until the array is sorted.

