A WPF Datatemplate is used to define a template for a data object that can be used to bind to a view model property. Here is an example of how to use a Datatemplate in WPF:

1. Create a new WPF project in Visual Studio.
2. Add a new class to your project that implements the INotifyPropertyChanged interface. This class will serve as your view model.
```csharp
public class MainViewModel : INotifyPropertyChanged
{
    private string _name;
    public string Name
    {
        get { return _name; }
        set
        {
            _name = value;
            OnPropertyChanged("Name");
        }
    }

    private string _age;
    public string Age
    {
        get { return _age; }
        set
        {
            _age = value;
            OnPropertyChanged("Age");
        }
    }

    public event PropertyChangedEventHandler PropertyChanged;

    protected void OnPropertyChanged(string propertyName)
    {
        PropertyChanged?.Invoke(this, new PropertyChangedEventArgs(propertyName));
    }
}
```
3. Create a new resource directory in your project, and add a new XML file called "MyDataTemplate.xaml".
```php
<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:local="clr-namespace:WpfApp1">

    <DataTemplate x:Key="MyDataTemplate">
        <StackPanel>
            <TextBlock Text="{Binding Name}" />
            <TextBlock Text="{Binding Age}" />
        </StackPanel>
    </DataTemplate>
</ResourceDictionary>
```
4. In your MainWindow.xaml, add a Grid to display the datatemplate
```php
<Grid>
    <Grid.Resources>
        <ResourceDictionary>
            <local:MyDataTemplate x:Key="MyDataTemplate"/>
        </ResourceDictionary>
    </Grid.Resources>
    <StackPanel>
        <ContentControl ContentTemplate="{StaticResource MyDataTemplate}" />
    </StackPanel>
</Grid>
```

